 "summary": "The ruled step 1 ran first and its stop condition fires on BOTH arms, so no repair code was written and no PR opened. (1) Readers outside the tier need the flag: react-page.tsx buildComponentScope needs a LAYOUT-containment signal that differs from the child-list reading exactly on button/badge/alert, and objectstack's save-gate copy of the parser reads isContainer out of sdui.manifest.json. (2) Registrations whose child-list reading cannot be derived at the tier: on the full registry (the 16 modules the manifest dump loads, plus @object-ui/layout) 74 distinct registrations put authored children on the page and only 9 of them (plus tooltip) publish a `children` input the tier can see. 65 publish it nowhere the tier reads: 15 only through isContainer, 50 not at all, and 2 more (sidebar, sidebar-menu-button) render children only inside their provider context. All ten converged registrations are in the underivable 50. The card's premise holds on origin/main 62597c5: the ten, tooltip, the five page kinds, sidebar and sidebar-menu-button all draw a FALSE not-a-container on `children`. What fails is the ruling's precondition that the tier can derive the reading.",
 "step1": {
  "base": "objectui origin/main 62597c588072636e9c30ea35b3d89b1e46fd765d (BASE); objectstack origin/main c1641868a3da71537c9c6c572d2bd2044103236b, whose .objectui-sha pin is the same 62597c5",
  "measured_at": "2026-09-24T05:50Z to 2026-09-24T05:56Z",
  "enumeration_command": "git grep -nw isContainer 62597c5 → exit 0, 170 lines in 69 files. Excluding tests, CHANGELOGs and .changeset: 27 files. A case-insensitive is_?container sweep adds only one test-local helper name.",
  "lit_control": "git grep -nw isContainer 62597c5 -- packages/layout/CHANGELOG.md → exit 0, 3 hits. Chosen because a published CHANGELOG is never re-addressed (objectui AGENTS.md section 11), so no repair can put this control out. Cross-repo twin: objectstack c1641868 packages/console/CHANGELOG.md → 2 hits. Same-token non-flag control: the PageBlockCanvas.tsx local variable (see readers) shows the grep is lexical, not filtered by meaning.",
  "readers": [
   {
    "at": "packages/sdui-parser/src/validate.ts, validateTree containment branch `if (node.children?.length && !comp.isContainer)` (L173 at 62597c5)",
    "role": "THE TIER",
    "needs_flag": "no, this is what the ruling replaces"
   },
   {
    "at": "packages/sdui-parser/src/validate.ts calls checkRetiredBodyDialect(node.type, key, value, comp.isContainer) (L105) → body-dialect.ts param isContainer (L71-75)",
    "role": "THE TIER (retired body dialect)",
    "needs_flag": "no, it follows whatever the containment branch reads"
   },
   {
    "at": "packages/components/src/renderers/layout/react-page.tsx buildComponentScope `if (!tag || cfg.isContainer) continue;` (L75-77)",
    "role": "OUTSIDE the tier: builds the injected JSX scope of every kind:'react' page",
    "needs_flag": "YES. Evidence: the public bare tags that render authored children are alert, badge, box, button, card, container, flex, grid, stack (probe). Swapping in a derived reads-children predicate here adds alert, badge and button to the skip set, which deletes the Alert/Badge/Button identifiers from every react page. That is the capability loss objectui#6804 ground (2) refused. Computed from the probe dump; not executed against react-page."
   },
   {
    "at": "objectstack packages/sdui-parser/src/validate.ts containment branch (same predicate, L168 at c1641868), reached from packages/lint/src/authoring-rules.ts rule validateJsxPages (tier 'gating') with ctx.sduiManifest resolved by packages/cli/src/utils/sdui-manifest.ts from @objectstack/console/dist/sdui.manifest.json",
    "role": "OUTSIDE the tier and cross-repo: the SAVE GATE copy of the parser, lockstep under objectstack#12719",
    "needs_flag": "YES as of today. The public-tier manifest is its only containment signal. In the tracked sdui.manifest.json (57 components), 10 carry isContainer and only 4 of those carry a `children` input (page:card/footer/section/sidebar), so it cannot derive containment for card, container, grid, stack, page:accordion or page:tabs. objectstack scripts/check-sdui-lockstep.mjs compares diagnostic codes and the parse.ts literal-subset region only, so an objectui-only predicate change would NOT turn it red, and the save gate and the renderer would silently disagree on not-a-container."
   },
   {
    "at": "packages/sdui-parser/src/index.ts RegistryConfigLike.isContainer (L72) + manifestFromConfigs projection `isContainer: c.isContainer` (L191); types.ts ManifestComponent.isContainer (L152)",
    "role": "published manifest shape and its producer. Feeds sdui.manifest.json (scripts/gen-manifest.ts, public tier) and so the reader above.",
    "needs_flag": "carrier, not a decider. Removing it breaks the save-gate reader above."
   },
   {
    "at": "packages/sdui-parser/src/codegen.ts generateBlockList Container column `c.isContainer ? '✓' : ''` (L176)",
    "role": "docs table in sdui-blocks.md",
    "needs_flag": "no. It could read the derived reading."
   },
   {
    "at": "packages/components/src/renderers/layout/page.tsx getJsxManifest projection (L481); packages/core/src/registry/WidgetRegistry.ts widget-manifest → registry config (L190)",
    "role": "projections. WidgetRegistry is the THIRD-PARTY widget path: WidgetManifest.isContainer flows into the registry.",
    "needs_flag": "carriers"
   },
   {
    "at": "packages/types/src/base.ts ComponentMeta.isContainer ('Whether the component can have children'); packages/types/src/widget.ts WidgetManifest.isContainer; packages/types/src/zod/base.zod.ts ComponentMetaSchema.isContainer ('Can have children'); skills/objectui/guides/plugin-development.md ('Accepts child components'); content/docs/guide/react-pages.md",
    "role": "PUBLISHED authoring declarations and docs of the flag's meaning",
    "needs_flag": "They declare the flag to plugin authors. Under C they become declared-but-unenforced for containment unless they are re-described or retired, which is a contract decision."
   },
   {
    "at": "apps/console/src/__tests__/public-contract.test.ts DECLARED_LAYOUT_CONTAINERS (`getMeta(type)?.isContainer === true`)",
    "role": "test reader (objectui#6879 PUBLIC_BLOCKS ledger)",
    "needs_flag": "yes, in its layout-containment meaning (same meaning as react-page)"
   },
   {
    "at": "packages/app-shell/src/views/metadata-admin/previews/PageBlockCanvas.tsx local `const isContainer`, computed from `childGroups(block).length` (L710)",
    "role": "local variable of the same name",
    "needs_flag": "NOT a flag reader (confirmed: computed from the block's child groups)"
   },
   {
    "at": "packages/sdui-parser/verify.ts fixtures; scripts/check-lucide-icon-record-names.mjs (header comment only); scripts/container-declaration-baseline.json note",
    "role": "dev script / prose",
    "needs_flag": "no"
   }
  ],
  "registrations": {
   "instrument": "Temporary probes, never committed: the ratchet's own runtime predicate (SchemaRenderer with one authored text child; did it reach the DOM), extended over every KNOWN key, with the tier's manifest built the way getJsxManifest builds it. Population A: packages/components only, which is the ratchet's population: 295 keys, 132 bare. Population B: the 16 eager modules apps/console/dev/manifest-dump.tsx loads, plus @object-ui/layout: 498 keys, 279 distinct registrations, 0 lazy, 0 unknown-component. A third probe re-ran the blind cases inside their provider context.",
   "full_registry_distinct": "74 registrations render authored children. 10 publish a `children` input the tier can see: page:card, page:footer, page:section, page:sidebar, ui:app, ui:home, ui:page, ui:record, ui:utility and ui:tooltip; tooltip is probe-blind (portal) and renders when open. 65 render children with NO child-list input: 15 of them only via isContainer, 50 via nothing.",
   "underivable_flagged_15_bare": "article, aside, aspect-ratio, box, card, container, flex, footer, grid, header, main, nav, page-header, section, stack. If the flag stopped deciding containment and the tier read inputs, each of these would start drawing a FALSE not-a-container, making the diagnostic weaker. The ruling forbids that.",
   "underivable_unflagged_50_bare": "the 44 baseline `undeclared` tags minus the 5 page kinds (39), plus the 11 `excluded` (button, alert, badge, 8 sidebar-*). All ten converged registrations are here.",
   "probe_blind_extra": "measured in provider context: sidebar TRUE, sidebar-menu-button TRUE, tooltip(open) TRUE, sidebar-trigger FALSE (control, it reads no children). So sidebar and sidebar-menu-button are a further under-count beyond comment 5732585445: they draw a false not-a-container, appear in neither baseline list, and are underivable. The ratchet's comment calling them not part of the cost is false for two of its three.",
   "flag_but_probe_negative": "page:accordion, page:tabs, responsive-grid, app-schema-renderer, layout:page:card. These declare isContainer but put no authored text child on the page under the bare probe. NOT MEASURED in context; in scope of the same derivation.",
   "zone3_mechanism_falsified": "Slot inputs cannot be the signal: 0 of the 65 underivable declare any slot input, and 10 registrations that read no `children` (alert-dialog, collapsible, context-menu, dialog, drawer, dropdown-menu, empty, hover-card, popover, sheet; their sources contain no schema.children) declare slot inputs, so a slot-based derivation would silence a TRUE diagnostic. The `body` input cannot be the signal either: the only registration declaring it is record:alert (string|object translation map), which renders no child list. Only an input NAMED `children` is sound, and 10 registrations carry one.",
   "baseline_reconciliation": "The ratchet and census are green at 62597c5 (2 files, 35 tests), so `undeclared` 44 + `excluded` 11 = 55 exactly equals today's runtime violators (render children, no flag). tooltip, sidebar and sidebar-menu-button are in neither list (probe-blind). The 5 page kinds sit in `undeclared` yet publish a `children` input (the page.tsx pageMeta `name: 'children', type: 'array'`), so they are the only baseline rows a derived reading can already clear."
  },
  "stop_condition": "FIRES on both arms: a reader outside the tier needs the flag (react-page; objectstack save gate), and 65 registrations (+2 context-only) have a child-list reading the tier cannot derive. Per the ruling, no fallback to the flag was invented; the route is returned for decision below."
 },
 "tests": "All heavy runs went through os-verify-lock (slot issue-9910-dev), each reading `VERDICT command-exit 0`. (1) `pnpm exec vitest run packages/components/src/renderers/__tests__/zz-9910-step1-probe.test.tsx` → 1 passed, 295 keys dumped. (2) `pnpm exec vitest run apps/console/src/__tests__/zz-9910-full-probe.test.tsx` → 1 passed, 498 keys. (3) `pnpm exec vitest run packages/components/src/renderers/__tests__/zz-9910-blind-probe.test.tsx` → 1 passed, the context readings above. (4) Control at BASE: `pnpm exec vitest run packages/components/src/renderers/__tests__/container-declaration-ratchet.test.tsx packages/components/src/renderers/__tests__/container-declaration-census.test.tsx` → Test Files 2 passed, Tests 35 passed. All three probe files were deleted and never committed: `git status --porcelain` shows 0 lines at HEAD 62597c5. No ablation: no repair was written.",
